(6393663, 945371, 98339, '<td valign="top">Allen this is amazing to say the least...superb job...one question...how many of the tubes did you use...all 3 or which one(s)???</td>', 'Allen this is amazing to say the least...superb job...one question...how many of the tubes did you use...all 3 or which one(s)???', '2011-04-23 19:35:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6393687, 945371, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ja-9:</b></div><hr/><i> Allen this is amazing to say the least...superb job...one question...how many of the tubes did you use...all 3 or which one(s)??? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you, Janine!  I used all 3 extension tubes hooked up together.  I always take the lens hood off when I use these tubes because when I use the tubes I get even closer to my subject that I normally would.  It takes some time getting used to them and in my experience a little harder to focus with them on than without them, but they provide amazing results on tiny subjects.</td>', 'Originally posted by Ja-9: Allen this is amazing to say the least...superb job...one question...how many of the tubes did you use...all 3 or which one(s)???   Thank you, Janine!  I used all 3 extension tubes hooked up together.  I always take the lens hood off when I use these tubes because when I use the tubes I get even closer to my subject that I normally would.  It takes some time getting used to them and in my experience a little harder to focus with them on than without them, but they provide amazing results on tiny subjects.', '2011-04-23 21:00:02.000000', NULL, 0),
